  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They outscored Baltimore 3-0 in the fifth and held on by one.",
    "what_this_means": "The window opened in the fifth. Nick Kurtz and Jacob Wilson found runs when it mattered most. Traffic became production when the leverage shifted. That's the only sequence that separated a one-run win from a one-run loss. Jacob Lopez gave them five innings of work, thin enough to require precision but enough to build on. The offense converted three of nine RISP situations. This is not abundance. This is math that only works if nothing else breaks. A one-run lead over four innings feels borrowed against a division opponent at home, and the Athletics held. The pitching didn't fold. The lead survived. That's not a pattern yet. It's a moment that mattered more because the margin is real.",
